# Performance — Physics and Jobs

- **Physics**: Use physics only where needed (ragdoll, collision, raycasts); avoid unnecessary rigidbodies or continuous collision checks.
- **Heavy math**: Use Burst and the Job System for terrain generation, pathfinding, or other CPU-heavy work; see `com.unity.burst`, `com.unity.collections`, `com.unity.mathematics` in `memory-bank/techContext.md`.
- **Avoid**: Blocking the main thread with large synchronous work; prefer incremental or job-based processing.
